merry christmas wishes for 2020  i like to keep things light-hearted at  christmas time  but we can't ignore that many of us have  had a difficult year  with illness uncertain employment  and isolation due to covert 19.  looking back at events of 2020  i felt extremely honoured to have been  chosen by my colleagues to continue to  serve as the chairman of rocha district  council  this is partly due to the cancellation  of the election  and the sad loss of my vice chairman  councillor terry cutmore  one of the greatest benefits of this  position is having the opportunity to  meet local residents or  and organizations that work so hard to  make a difference around our district  this year has been different and i've  missed meeting many local residents and  visiting local businesses  virtual meetings have become the norm  for most of us and i am no different  from a screen i have attended not only  council meetings but events in the  community such as a conscious demeanor  making ceremony  and havens light up a life event  it is humbling to see how olville  adapted to this new way of working  the highlight of 2020 has been the  community  response to the covid 19 pandemic the  rocha district community hub is a great  reminder of what the community can do  when we all work together we've had over  200 volunteers delivering food and  medicine  and offering reassurance to residents in  need  this hub is an asset to the community  and continues to help those in need  my own civic carol service was unable to  go ahead this year at the holy trinity  church in raleigh  i would like to give special thanks to  chairman's chaplain reverend david  oxtoby who has put together a virtual  service  which i will be taking part in and will  take place  on saturday the 19th of december at 7 pm  i also want to send thanks to the key  workers of workers who have worked  tirelessly throughout this difficult  year  to those who have worked in our schools  collected our waste and kept services  running  i will be joining in with a bell ringing  from my doorstep at 6 00 pm on christmas  eve to show my thanks  over the next six months of my  chairmanship i look forward to seeing  more of our residents and businesses  and to celebrating the successes to come  in a new year  i will be thrilled to be present to  support you and join in with celebrating  your achievements  so if you would like to invite me to  share an event with you please contact  the civic officer  by email at civic.officer  rochford.gov dot uk or visit the  chairman's page on the rocha district  council website  to download an engagement form  stay safe this christmas while indulging  in your minch pies  please stick to the rules in place while  you enjoy spending time with loved ones  i'll be seeing my mother for the first  time in many months  which i'm very much looking forward to i  wish you all a merry christmas and best  wishes for a happy and safe 2021.
 

